# Cline Rules for Leaflet

## Project Overview
Leaflet is an open-source JavaScript library for mobile-friendly interactive maps (~40 kB gzipped JS + 3.2 kB gzipped CSS). It emphasises simplicity, performance and usability.

## Code Style
- Use tabs for indentation and spaces for alignment.
- Use ES module syntax (import/export). Always include .js file extensions in import paths.
- Always use curly braces for control structures (if, else, for, etc.).
- Comments must have a space after // or /*.
- Prefer ** over Math.pow() and Object.hasOwn() over hasOwnProperty.
- No unused variables (caught errors in catch blocks are exempt).
- Run `npm run lint` before committing.

## Project Structure
- src/ - Library source code (core/, dom/, geo/, geometry/, layer/, map/, control/).
- spec/suites/ - Tests (Mocha + Chai, run via Karma).
- dist/ - Generated build output. Do not edit.
- build/ - Build scripts (Rollup, Leafdoc).
- docs/ - Jekyll documentation site.

## Key Patterns
- Custom OOP: Class.extend(), Class.include(), Class.mergeOptions().
- Events: Evented mixin with on(), off(), fire(), listens().
- Options: Static options object merged via L.Util.setOptions().
- DOM: Use src/dom/ utilities rather than direct DOM manipulation.

## Commands
- Install: `npm install`
- Build: `npm run build`
- Lint: `npm run lint`
- Fix lint: `npm run lintfix`
- Test: `npm test -- --single-run` (requires Chrome)
- Watch: `npm run watch`
- Docs: `npm run docs`

## Guidelines
- Keep changes small and focused; Leaflet values simplicity and small bundle size.
- Ensure broad browser compatibility (baseline-js/use-baseline ESLint rules).
- Build the project before running tests.
- API docs come from Leafdoc comments in source files - edit those to update docs.
- Always use topic branches, never commit directly to main.
